  "generated_text": "We are given $e^{i \\alpha} + e^{i \\beta} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{3}{7} i.$\nWe want to find $e^{-i \\alpha} + e^{-i \\beta}.$\nRecall that $e^{-i \\theta} = \\cos(\\theta) - i \\sin(\\theta)$ for any angle $\\theta.$\nSo, $e^{-i \\alpha} + e^{-i \\beta} = (\\cos(\\alpha) - i \\sin(\\alpha)) + (\\cos(\\beta) - i \\sin(\\beta)) = \\cos(\\alpha) + \\cos(\\beta) - i (\\sin(\\alpha) + \\sin(\\beta)).$\n\nFrom the given equation, we can see that $\\cos(\\alpha) + \\cos(\\beta) = \\frac{1}{4}$ and $\\sin(\\alpha) + \\sin(\\beta) = \\frac{3}{7}.$\nTherefore, $e^{-i \\alpha} + e^{-i \\beta} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{3}{7} i}.$\nThe answer is: \\frac{1}{4}",
